# Design System Rules

Read `DESIGN.md`, `.ai/context/design-system.md`, and `.ai/patterns/ui-composition.md` before any UI work.
For broad polish, landing pages, or premium-feel UI review, also read `.ai/skills/anti-slop-ui.md`.

## Key reminders

- Preserve the mature neutral shadcn-style baseline unless a palette change is explicitly requested.
- Use shared theme tokens instead of hardcoded colors.
- Use CVA, `cn()`, named exports, and `data-slot` for shared UI components.
- Avoid nested cards and decorative-only layouts in app workflows.
- Update `DESIGN.md` in the same commit as any runtime token change.
- Run `pnpm design:lint`, `pnpm design:tokens`, and `pnpm ui:composition`
  before completing UI work.
